From 2ea7c90a8cb1add215fcc78ba82f5530f4d62906 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:35:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] BRAKE-AXIS: servo ON 0.5 s -> that axis' own brake output
 released; servo OFF -> brake held first
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260929: "只要SERVO ON 就必須要先激磁 0.5秒後 觸發io的煞車" / "寫在激磁 只要有激磁做動 0.5秒 就要觸發對應io煞車
如果有煞車io的話". Measured before: MInArmZA servo ON at 20:20:27, but the golden group release (InOutArmZ) waited for
MOutArmZA too, so SwInArmZBreaker stayed held while MoveN drove the axis.

- WebMotorAccessLive.cpp BrakeAxisTick (after every monitor Poll, also in the modal wait loop): per axis
  MInArmZA/SwInArmZBreaker, MOutArmZA/SwOutArmZBreaker, MTestZ1/SwFMotorBreaker, MTestZ2/SwBMotorBreaker,
  MLoaderZ/SwCassetteLDMotBreaker, MAuto1Z/SwCassetteAuto1MotBreaker, MAuto2Z/SwCassetteAuto2MotBreaker
  (only an Enable=1 output and an enabled PCI1203 row opened by the monitor):
  SVON seen -> 0.5 s later the output ON (release) once, if motor power is on and no EMG;
  SVON gone (drive alarm ...) -> the output OFF (hold) at once.
- Motor Test / teach servo OFF: BrakeHoldBeforeServoOff, 100 ms, then Acm_AxSetSvOn 0; no release for 1 s after a hold.
- The golden group releases (G05 / G16 / HOME start) now also need every axis of the group SVON for 0.5 s.
- op log: BRAKE lines (g_W906BrakeNote); console: [brake] lines.
- Not driven: SwCassetteEmptyMotBreaker (MEmptyZ) and SwCassetteAuto3MotBreaker (MAuto3Z) are in IO_Table but have no
  SW[] in this program.
- tests: test_web_motor_access 547 passed / 0 failed (scratch build).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
